{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 16, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a member of the House of Poitiers and the ruler of the County of Tripoli from 1152 until his death in 1187. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem and the grandson of Raymond II's predecessor Bohemond II of Antioch.\n\n* **Early Life and Succession** *\n\nRaymond III was born in 1140 and succeeded his father as Count of Tripoli in 1152 at the age of 12. He was not yet 12 when he was taken to the Kingdom of Jerusalem to be educated. His mother Hodierna of Jerusalem played a significant role in his upbringing and the early years of his rule.\n\n* **Marriage and Children** *\n\nRaymond III married Eschiva of Bures and had three children with her. His first son was Bohemond III who succeeded him as Count of Tripoli. He also had two daughters with Eschiva. \n\nThe County of Tripoli was under threat from the Ayyubid dynasty of Egypt and the Zengid dynasty of Mosul. Raymond III formed an alliance with the Kingdom of Jerusalem and the Principality of Antioch to counter these threats. He also maintained good relations with the Byzantine Empire.\n\n* **Battle of Hattin and Death** *\n\nRaymond III was present at the Battle of Hattin in 1187 where the Kingdom of Jerusalem was defeated by the Ayyubid forces led by Saladin. Raymond III managed to escape from the battlefield and fled to the County of Tripoli. However he died shortly after the battle in 1187. He was succeeded by his son Bohemond III who went on to play a significant role in the Third Crusade.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {"token": " was", "l